The plate is a square dinner plate, about 24 cm across. The corn piece measures roughly 75 px by 90 px, and the plate spans about 430 px. That puts the corn at about 4 cm by 5 cm, so it is a short corn cob segment about 4 cm long and 4.5 cm in diameter.

Its volume is π × 2.25² × 4 ≈ 64 cm³. Cob is included, and kernels on a cob weigh about 0.7 g/cm³ overall, giving roughly 45–50 g. I'll use 50 g. Boiled corn on the cob is about 96 kcal per 100 g.

